.TH BRK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
brk \- request a new program break
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int brk(void* address);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Requests a new end address for the process data segment. This is a low\-level
Linux interface; changing the break can conflict with libc or any other
allocator using it. The caller must coordinate all break users.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero when the kernel break is at or above the requested address.
Otherwise returns \-1 and sets errno to ENOMEM. Success leaves errno unchanged.
The kernel may decline a request to shrink the break, in which case this
glibc\-style return convention can still report success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brk (2)
